=== SURVEY ===

Baseline before edits:

  Backend vehicle data source for the new AI surface:
    GET /api/v1/vehicles/{vehicleID}           → internal/api/vehicle_handler.go
    GET /api/v1/vehicles/{vehicleID}/config    → internal/api/vehicle_config_handler.go
    Returns deterministic Vehicle + VehicleConfig records
    (model, trim_level, exterior_color, wheel_type, etc.). No
    AI involvement; the only mutation paths are the existing
    typed PUT/POST handlers under /api/v1/vehicles/* and
    /api/v1/settings/* — both unchanged by this slice.

  Frontend canonical baseline surface for vehicle appearance:
    /vehicles/:vehicleId  → web/src/features/vehicles/pages/VehicleDetailPage.tsx
    Renders VehicleHeader, BatteryRangePanel, LiveStateIndicators,
    QuickStatsGrid, MotorSection, ClimateSection, SecuritySection,
    TirePressureSection, ChargingTelemetrySection,
    BatteryRangeCharts, RecentDrivesSection, RecentChargesSection,
    VehicleConfigSection (the model/trim/exterior-color +
    software-version surface), QuickLinksSection, and the per-
    vehicle VehicleSettingsTab. The deterministic vehicle
    photos + manual theme/appearance settings flow through this
    surface and are NOT touched by this slice.

  Vehicle source for the strategy:
    internal/database/vehicle_repo.go → VehicleRepo with
    GetByID(ctx, id) returning *models.Vehicle. The AI handler
    treats this as a read-only data plane and never invokes the
    typed mutation handlers from the LLM execution path.

  Existing AI surfaces this slice is modeled after:
